IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ica-dates`

-- Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA), Part 7A (child abuse: liability of institutions) and Part 7B (child abuse: setting
-- aside settlements), inserted by the Civil Liability (Institutional Child Abuse Liability) Amendment Act 2021, in
-- operation from 1 August 2022. These, with s 3A of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936 (no limitation period for child
-- abuse actions, encoded in that Act's own baseline), are South Australia's equivalents of the reforms other
-- jurisdictions made after the Royal Commission into Institutional Responses to Child Sexual Abuse. Seat-neutral: every
-- rule is here, and the seat of the person abused as a child (ica-seat.l4) asks the questions. One regulative rule
-- (s 50J(7)(a), the court's order to identify associated trusts within 28 days) is run by EVALTRACE.
--
-- Answers are named outcomes. Where the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, an "if" that fails, "does
-- not apply", "must not", "may only ... if") the outcome begins "no:"; where the text lists without closing the list
-- ("includes") the outcome says "the Act does not say"; where a scope limit without "only" is not met the outcome says
-- the Division "does not reach this" (the 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 rulings in substance). A court's judgment ("all
-- reasonable steps", "supplied the occasion", "just and reasonable", "appropriate", "satisfied") is an input, never
-- decided here.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025 (the Act as at 22 June 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Liability Act 1936 Parts 7A and 7B -- child abuse claims against institutions`

§§ `s 50A, s 50C -- abuse, child, institution, persons associated, abuse claim`

-- s 50A(1): "abuse, of a child, includes any of the following: (a) sexual abuse of the child; (b) serious physical abuse
-- of the child; (c) psychological abuse of the child related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the child".
-- The list is not closed, so a kind outside it is not answered.
DECLARE `Kind of abuse` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`
    `physical abuse that was not serious`
    `psychological abuse not related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`
    `another kind of abuse`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of abuse`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a kind of abuse the Act lists` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `sexual abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `serious physical abuse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `psychological abuse related to sexual abuse or serious physical abuse` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 50A(1): "child means a person under 18 years of age".
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a child at age` `the age` IF `the age` LESS THAN 18

-- s 50C(1): "the persons associated with an institution include -- (a) an officer, office holder, representative,
-- leader, owner, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of the institution; and (b) for an institution that is a
-- religious organisation -- a minister of religion, religious leader or member of the personnel of the organisation; and
-- (c) if the institution has delegated the care, supervision, control or authority over a child to another entity (the
-- delegate) -- (i) if the delegate is an individual -- the delegate; and (ii) a person who would be a person mentioned in
-- paragraph (a) or (b) if the delegate were the delegating institution; and (d) a designated carer (other than a
-- designated carer who is the parent or guardian of the child ...); and (e) a person, or person of a class, prescribed by
-- regulation." s 50C(2): "A person is not associated with an institution only because the person is associated with an
-- entity that is funded or regulated by the institution."
DECLARE `Connection with the institution` IS ONE OF
    `an officer, office holder, representative, leader, owner, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of the institution`
    `a minister of religion, religious leader or member of the personnel of the institution, a religious organisation`
    `the individual to whom the institution delegated the care, supervision, control or authority over me`
    `an officer, office holder, representative, leader, owner, employee, agent, volunteer or contractor of the entity to which the institution delegated my care`
    `a designated carer with whom I was placed, not my parent or guardian`
    `a designated carer with whom I was placed, who was my parent or guardian`
    `a person associated only with an entity that the institution funds or regulates`
    `some other connection`

DECLARE `Association` IS ONE OF
    `associated`
    `not associated`
    `not settled by the Act`

-- Fork F3: the designated carer who is the child's parent or guardian is carved out of paragraph (d) by "(other than
-- ...)", but the list "includes" and is not closed, so the encoding does not say no. Fork F4: a person prescribed by
-- regulation (s 50C(1)(e)) falls under "some other connection", because no regulation made under Part 7A is deposited.
GIVEN c IS A `Connection with the institution`
GIVETH AN `Association`
`the association of` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a designated carer with whom I was placed, who was my parent or guardian` THEN `not settled by the Act`
    WHEN `a person associated only with an entity that the institution funds or regulates` THEN `not associated`
    WHEN `some other connection` THEN `not settled by the Act`
    OTHERWISE `associated`

-- One case: one person abused as a child, one institution, one abuser.
DECLARE `Abuse facts` HAS
    `the age when abused` IS A NUMBER
    `the abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`
    `the body was responsible for the child and gave contact with children` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the body is a family` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the abuser's connection` IS A `Connection with the institution`
    `the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 50A(1): "abuse claim means a claim arising from the abuse of a child by a person associated with an institution
-- while the child was under the care, supervision, control or authority of the institution"; "institution -- (a) means
-- an entity (whether private or public) that is responsible for a child and provides an activity, program or service of
-- a kind that gives an opportunity for a person to have contact with a child; and (b) does not include a family".
DECLARE `Abuse claim answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an abuse claim, a claim arising from the abuse of a child by a person associated with an institution while the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority (s 50A(1))`
    `no: "child" means a person under 18 years of age (s 50A(1)), and you were 18 or over`
    `no: an institution means an entity, private or public, that is responsible for a child and provides an activity, program or service giving a person an opportunity for contact with a child (s 50A(1), "institution" (a))`
    `no: an institution does not include a family (s 50A(1), "institution" (b))`
    `no: an abuse claim needs the abuse to have happened while you were under the institution's care, supervision, control or authority (s 50A(1))`
    `no: a person is not associated with an institution only because they are associated with an entity the institution funds or regulates (s 50C(2))`
    `the Act does not say: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 50A(1)), and the list is not closed`
    `the Act does not say: the persons associated with an institution "include" those listed in s 50C(1), and the list is not closed`

GIVEN f IS AN `Abuse facts`
GIVETH AN `Abuse claim answer`
`the abuse claim answer for` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`a child at age` (f's `the age when abused`)))
        THEN `no: "child" means a person under 18 years of age (s 50A(1)), and you were 18 or over`
        IF (NOT (f's `the body was responsible for the child and gave contact with children`))
        THEN `no: an institution means an entity, private or public, that is responsible for a child and provides an activity, program or service giving a person an opportunity for contact with a child (s 50A(1), "institution" (a))`
        IF f's `the body is a family`
        THEN `no: an institution does not include a family (s 50A(1), "institution" (b))`
        IF (NOT (f's `the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority`))
        THEN `no: an abuse claim needs the abuse to have happened while you were under the institution's care, supervision, control or authority (s 50A(1))`
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the association of` (f's `the abuser's connection`)
             WHEN `not associated` THEN `no: a person is not associated with an institution only because they are associated with an entity the institution funds or regulates (s 50C(2))`
             WHEN `not settled by the Act` THEN
                 IF `is a kind of abuse the Act lists` (f's `the abuse`)
                 THEN `the Act does not say: the persons associated with an institution "include" those listed in s 50C(1), and the list is not closed`
                 ELSE `the Act does not say: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 50A(1)), and the list is not closed`
             OTHERWISE
                 IF `is a kind of abuse the Act lists` (f's `the abuse`)
                 THEN `yes: an abuse claim, a claim arising from the abuse of a child by a person associated with an institution while the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority (s 50A(1))`
                 ELSE `the Act does not say: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 50A(1)), and the list is not closed`

DECLARE `Claim status` IS ONE OF
    `an abuse claim`
    `not an abuse claim`
    `not settled by the Act whether it is an abuse claim`

GIVEN f IS AN `Abuse facts`
GIVETH A `Claim status`
`the claim status of` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `the abuse claim answer for` f
    WHEN `yes: an abuse claim, a claim arising from the abuse of a child by a person associated with an institution while the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority (s 50A(1))` THEN `an abuse claim`
    WHEN `the Act does not say: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 50A(1)), and the list is not closed` THEN `not settled by the Act whether it is an abuse claim`
    WHEN `the Act does not say: the persons associated with an institution "include" those listed in s 50C(1), and the list is not closed` THEN `not settled by the Act whether it is an abuse claim`
    OTHERWISE `not an abuse claim`

-- A judgment the Act leaves to the court, asked as where it stands.
DECLARE `Court finding` IS ONE OF
    `the court has found that it is so`
    `the court has found that it is not so`
    `the court has not decided yet`

§§ `s 50A(1), (2) -- employee, and akin to an employee`

-- s 50A(1): "employee, of an institution, includes a person who is akin to an employee of the institution". s 50A(2):
-- "a person is akin to an employee of an institution if the person carries out activities as an integral part of the
-- activities carried on by the institution and does so for the benefit of the institution, but a person is not akin to
-- an employee if -- (a) the activities are carried out for a recognisably independent business of the person or of
-- another person or institution; or (b) the activities carried on by the person are the activities of a designated carer
-- carried on in the person's capacity as a designated carer." "Employee" in its ordinary sense is borrowed and asked.
-- s 50A(3) (regulations may prescribe otherwise): no such regulation is deposited (fork F4).
DECLARE `Employment facts` HAS
    `an employee in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activities were an integral part of the institution's` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they were for the institution's benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they were for a recognisably independent business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they were a designated carer's activities as a designated carer` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Employee answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an employee of the institution`
    `yes: akin to an employee, and so an employee of the institution for Part 7A (s 50A(1), (2))`
    `no: not akin to an employee, because the activities were carried out for a recognisably independent business (s 50A(2)(a))`
    `no: not akin to an employee, because the activities were those of a designated carer, carried on as a designated carer (s 50A(2)(b))`
    `no: not an employee, and not akin to one, which needs activities carried out as an integral part of the institution's activities and for its benefit (s 50A(2))`

GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`
GIVETH AN `Employee answer`
`the employee answer for` e MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF e's `an employee in the ordinary sense`
        THEN `yes: an employee of the institution`
        IF (NOT (e's `the activities were an integral part of the institution's` AND e's `they were for the institution's benefit`))
        THEN `no: not an employee, and not akin to one, which needs activities carried out as an integral part of the institution's activities and for its benefit (s 50A(2))`
        IF e's `they were for a recognisably independent business`
        THEN `no: not akin to an employee, because the activities were carried out for a recognisably independent business (s 50A(2)(a))`
        IF e's `they were a designated carer's activities as a designated carer`
        THEN `no: not akin to an employee, because the activities were those of a designated carer, carried on as a designated carer (s 50A(2)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: akin to an employee, and so an employee of the institution for Part 7A (s 50A(1), (2))`

GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an employee for Part 7A` e MEANS
    CONSIDER `the employee answer for` e
    WHEN `yes: an employee of the institution` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `yes: akin to an employee, and so an employee of the institution for Part 7A (s 50A(1), (2))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 50D -- which causes of action Part 7A reaches`

-- s 50D(1): "This Part, other than Division 2 and Division 3, applies in relation to a cause of action whether it arose
-- before or after the commencement of this Part." Divisions 2 and 3 are left out, so for abuse before 1 August 2022 the
-- encoding says they "do not reach this on their words" (finding 1; fork F2: the cause of action is taken to arise on the
-- day of the abuse). s 50D(2) binds the Crown, so a public institution is reached like a private one.
GIVEN `the abuse day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Divisions 2 and 3 reach abuse on` `the abuse day` IF
    (NOT (`the abuse day` `is before` `the commencement of Part 7A`))

§§ `ss 50E, 50F -- the duty to prevent child abuse, and the reversed onus`

-- s 50E(1): "An institution has a duty to take all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse of a child by a person
-- associated with the institution while the child is under the care, supervision, control or authority of the
-- institution." (2): it "does not apply to abuse ... in circumstances wholly unrelated to that person's association with
-- the institution." (3): where the care was delegated to another institution, it "does not apply to abuse of the child
-- by a person associated with the delegate institution in circumstances wholly unrelated to that person's association
-- with the delegator institution or the delegate institution" (fork F5: unrelated to both). s 50F(2): "The institution
-- is taken to have breached its duty under section 50E unless the institution proves it took all reasonable steps to
-- prevent the abuse." Whether it proved that is the court's judgment, weighing s 50F(3).
DECLARE `Duty facts` HAS
    `the abuse facts` IS AN `Abuse facts`
    `the day of the abuse` IS A DATE
    `wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with the institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the care was delegated and the abuser was associated with the delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with either institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the institution proved it took all reasonable steps` IS A `Court finding`

DECLARE `Duty answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the institution is taken to have breached its duty to take all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse, because it has not proved that it took them (ss 50E(1), 50F(2))`
    `no: the institution proved that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse, so it is not taken to have breached its duty (s 50F(2))`
    `yes, unless the institution proves that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse (s 50F(2)); the court weighs the matters in s 50F(3)`
    `no: the duty does not apply to abuse in circumstances wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with the institution (s 50E(2))`
    `no: your care was delegated to another institution, and the duty does not apply to abuse by a person associated with the delegate in circumstances wholly unrelated to that person's association with either institution (s 50E(3))`
    `Division 2 does not reach this on its words: s 50D(1) applies Part 7A to causes of action that arose before 1 August 2022 but leaves Divisions 2 and 3 out; the general law of negligence still applies`
    `Division 2 does not reach this: on these facts the claim is not an abuse claim (see the abuse claim question)`
    `the Act does not say: whether this is an abuse claim turns on an open list in s 50A or s 50C (see the abuse claim question)`

GIVEN d IS A `Duty facts`
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
`the duty answer for` d MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim status of` (d's `the abuse facts`)
    WHEN `not an abuse claim` THEN `Division 2 does not reach this: on these facts the claim is not an abuse claim (see the abuse claim question)`
    WHEN `not settled by the Act whether it is an abuse claim` THEN `the Act does not say: whether this is an abuse claim turns on an open list in s 50A or s 50C (see the abuse claim question)`
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            IF (NOT (`Divisions 2 and 3 reach abuse on` (d's `the day of the abuse`)))
            THEN `Division 2 does not reach this on its words: s 50D(1) applies Part 7A to causes of action that arose before 1 August 2022 but leaves Divisions 2 and 3 out; the general law of negligence still applies`
            IF d's `wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with the institution`
            THEN `no: the duty does not apply to abuse in circumstances wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with the institution (s 50E(2))`
            IF d's `the care was delegated and the abuser was associated with the delegate` AND d's `wholly unrelated to the abuser's association with either institution`
            THEN `no: your care was delegated to another institution, and the duty does not apply to abuse by a person associated with the delegate in circumstances wholly unrelated to that person's association with either institution (s 50E(3))`
            OTHERWISE CONSIDER d's `the institution proved it took all reasonable steps`
                 WHEN `the court has found that it is so` THEN `no: the institution proved that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse, so it is not taken to have breached its duty (s 50F(2))`
                 WHEN `the court has found that it is not so` THEN `yes: the institution is taken to have breached its duty to take all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse, because it has not proved that it took them (ss 50E(1), 50F(2))`
                 OTHERWISE `yes, unless the institution proves that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse (s 50F(2)); the court weighs the matters in s 50F(3)`

§§ `s 50G -- vicarious liability for abuse by an employee`

-- s 50G(1): "An institution is vicariously liable for abuse of a child by an employee of the institution if -- (a) the
-- apparent performance by the employee of a role in which the institution placed the employee supplies the occasion for
-- the abuse of the child by the employee; and (b) the employee takes advantage of that occasion to abuse the child; and
-- (c) the abuse occurred while the child was under the care, supervision, control or authority of the institution."
-- (2) lists what the court takes into account for (a); (3) the common law is unaffected. An "if" that fails is this
-- section's no; the common law answer is not given here.
DECLARE `Vicarious facts` HAS
    `the abuse facts` IS AN `Abuse facts`
    `the employment facts` IS AN `Employment facts`
    `the day of the abuse` IS A DATE
    `the role supplied the occasion` IS A `Court finding`
    `the employee took advantage of that occasion` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Vicarious answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the institution is vicariously liable for the abuse (s 50G(1)), in addition to any liability at common law (s 50G(3))`
    `yes, if the court finds that the apparent performance of the role in which the institution placed the employee supplied the occasion for the abuse (s 50G(1)(a)); it takes into account whether the role gave the employee authority, power or control over you, your trust, or the ability to achieve intimacy with you (s 50G(2))`
    `no: s 50G makes an institution vicariously liable only for abuse by an employee, or a person akin to one (s 50G(1), s 50A(2)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
    `no: s 50G needs the abuse to have happened while you were under the institution's care, supervision, control or authority (s 50G(1)(c)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
    `no: s 50G needs the employee to have taken advantage of the occasion the role supplied (s 50G(1)(b)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
    `no: the court found that the role did not supply the occasion for the abuse (s 50G(1)(a)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
    `no: s 50G covers the abuse of a child, a person under 18 (s 50A(1))`
    `no: s 50G makes an institution liable, and an institution means an entity responsible for a child that provides an activity, program or service giving contact with children, and not a family (s 50A(1))`
    `Division 3 does not reach this on its words: s 50D(1) applies Part 7A to causes of action that arose before 1 August 2022 but leaves Divisions 2 and 3 out; the common law of vicarious liability still applies`
    `the Act does not say whether s 50G reaches this: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 50A(1)), and the list is not closed`

GIVEN v IS A `Vicarious facts`
GIVETH A `Vicarious answer`
`the vicarious answer for` v MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`a child at age` (v's `the abuse facts`'s `the age when abused`)))
        THEN `no: s 50G covers the abuse of a child, a person under 18 (s 50A(1))`
        IF (NOT (v's `the abuse facts`'s `the body was responsible for the child and gave contact with children`)) OR v's `the abuse facts`'s `the body is a family`
        THEN `no: s 50G makes an institution liable, and an institution means an entity responsible for a child that provides an activity, program or service giving contact with children, and not a family (s 50A(1))`
        IF (NOT (`Divisions 2 and 3 reach abuse on` (v's `the day of the abuse`)))
        THEN `Division 3 does not reach this on its words: s 50D(1) applies Part 7A to causes of action that arose before 1 August 2022 but leaves Divisions 2 and 3 out; the common law of vicarious liability still applies`
        IF (NOT (`is an employee for Part 7A` (v's `the employment facts`)))
        THEN `no: s 50G makes an institution vicariously liable only for abuse by an employee, or a person akin to one (s 50G(1), s 50A(2)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
        IF (NOT (v's `the abuse facts`'s `the child was under its care, supervision, control or authority`))
        THEN `no: s 50G needs the abuse to have happened while you were under the institution's care, supervision, control or authority (s 50G(1)(c)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
        IF (NOT (v's `the employee took advantage of that occasion`))
        THEN `no: s 50G needs the employee to have taken advantage of the occasion the role supplied (s 50G(1)(b)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER v's `the role supplied the occasion`
             WHEN `the court has found that it is not so` THEN `no: the court found that the role did not supply the occasion for the abuse (s 50G(1)(a)); the common law still applies (s 50G(3))`
             OTHERWISE
                 IF (NOT (`is a kind of abuse the Act lists` (v's `the abuse facts`'s `the abuse`)))
                 THEN `the Act does not say whether s 50G reaches this: abuse "includes" sexual abuse, serious physical abuse and psychological abuse related to them (s 50A(1)), and the list is not closed`
                 ELSE CONSIDER v's `the role supplied the occasion`
                      WHEN `the court has found that it is so` THEN `yes: the institution is vicariously liable for the abuse (s 50G(1)), in addition to any liability at common law (s 50G(3))`
                      OTHERWISE `yes, if the court finds that the apparent performance of the role in which the institution placed the employee supplied the occasion for the abuse (s 50G(1)(a)); it takes into account whether the role gave the employee authority, power or control over you, your trust, or the ability to achieve intimacy with you (s 50G(2))`

§§ `ss 50H-50K, 50S -- whom an abuse claim may be brought against`

-- s 50H: an institution unincorporated when the cause of action accrued and incorporated now may be sued in place of the
-- former office holder, or on the claim that lay against it under s 50J, if the claimant "is able to maintain
-- proceedings ..., or would be able to ... if the former office holder still held the relevant office" or "if the
-- institution was still an unincorporated body" (s 50H(1)(e)). s 50I: an institution unincorporated then and now; the
-- former office holder no longer holds the office; the current holder may be sued in the name of the office; s 50S(3):
-- with no office substantially the same, the current head. s 50J(2): "A proceeding for an abuse claim may be commenced
-- against the institution", (3) notice of the claim "must be given to the head of the institution in accordance with any
-- requirements prescribed by the regulations" (none deposited). s 50K: the nominee may be sued in its place.
DECLARE `Defendant facts` HAS
    `it was incorporated when the cause of action accrued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is incorporated now` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim is against a former office holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the former office holder still holds the office` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proceedings could be maintained but for the change` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the institution has a nominee` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Defendant route` IS ONE OF
    `the institution itself, which was already incorporated when the cause of action accrued: Division 4 does not reach this, and the ordinary law applies`
    `the institution, now incorporated, in place of the former office holder: it takes over their liability, acts, duties, defences and right to indemnity (s 50H(2), (3))`
    `the institution, now incorporated, on the claim that lay against it while it was unincorporated (s 50H(1)(b)(ii), (2))`
    `no route under s 50H: it applies only if you could maintain the proceedings had nothing changed (s 50H(1)(e))`
    `the current holder of the office of authority, in the name of the office, in place of the former office holder (s 50I(2), (3)); if no office is substantially the same, the current head of the institution (s 50S(3))`
    `the unincorporated institution itself, with notice of the claim to its head as the regulations require (s 50J(2), (3))`
    `the institution's nominee, which takes on the institution's liability, while the institution must still take part (s 50K)`

GIVEN d IS A `Defendant facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Defendant route`
`the routes for` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF d's `it was incorporated when the cause of action accrued`
        THEN LIST `the institution itself, which was already incorporated when the cause of action accrued: Division 4 does not reach this, and the ordinary law applies`
        IF d's `it is incorporated now` AND (NOT (d's `proceedings could be maintained but for the change`))
        THEN LIST `no route under s 50H: it applies only if you could maintain the proceedings had nothing changed (s 50H(1)(e))`
        IF d's `it is incorporated now` AND d's `the claim is against a former office holder`
        THEN LIST `the institution, now incorporated, in place of the former office holder: it takes over their liability, acts, duties, defences and right to indemnity (s 50H(2), (3))`
        IF d's `it is incorporated now`
        THEN LIST `the institution, now incorporated, on the claim that lay against it while it was unincorporated (s 50H(1)(b)(ii), (2))`
        OTHERWISE `the unincorporated institution itself, with notice of the claim to its head as the regulations require (s 50J(2), (3))` FOLLOWED BY `the further routes`
    WHERE
        `the nominee routes` MEANS
            IF d's `the institution has a nominee`
            THEN LIST `the institution's nominee, which takes on the institution's liability, while the institution must still take part (s 50K)`
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the further routes` MEANS
            IF d's `the claim is against a former office holder` AND (NOT (d's `the former office holder still holds the office`)) AND d's `proceedings could be maintained but for the change`
            THEN `the current holder of the office of authority, in the name of the office, in place of the former office holder (s 50I(2), (3)); if no office is substantially the same, the current head of the institution (s 50S(3))` FOLLOWED BY `the nominee routes`
            ELSE `the nominee routes`

§§ `s 50R -- is today's institution the one that is liable`

-- s 50R(1): "For the purposes of Division 4, it is sufficient that an institution ... is substantially the same as it was
-- at the time when the cause of action accrued"; (2) it is if "the class or type of member and the primary purposes or
-- work ... are substantially the same"; (3) a change of name, structure, incorporation or area does not matter; (4), (5)
-- a "relevant successor" (merger into, merger forming, the remainder, or a chain of these) is taken to be the same
-- institution; (6) several successors are jointly and severally liable, with contribution between them.
DECLARE `What became of the institution` IS ONE OF
    `it continues, perhaps with a new name, structure, incorporation or area`
    `all or part of it merged into another institution`
    `all or part of it merged with other entities to form a new institution`
    `part of it left, and the remainder continues as an institution`
    `a chain of such mergers, remainders and continuations leads to today's institution`
    `it ceased, with no successor`

DECLARE `Continuity answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: today's institution is the same institution, as the class or type of its members and its primary purposes or work are substantially the same (s 50R(1), (2)), whatever changed in its name, structure, incorporation or area (s 50R(3))`
    `yes, if the court finds today's institution substantially the same as it was when the cause of action accrued (s 50R(1)); the sufficient test of s 50R(2) is not met on these facts`
    `yes: today's institution is a relevant successor of the old institution, and is taken to be the same institution (s 50R(4), (5))`
    `yes: each of the relevant successors is jointly and severally liable for the abuse, and each may recover contribution from the others (s 50R(6))`
    `the Act does not say: with no institution the same or substantially the same, and no relevant successor, s 50R names no one`

GIVEN `what became of it` IS A `What became of the institution`
      `the members are substantially the same` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purposes are substantially the same` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of successors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Continuity answer`
`the continuity answer for` `what became of it` `members` `the members are substantially the same` `purposes` `the purposes are substantially the same` `successors` `the number of successors` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what became of it`
    WHEN `it continues, perhaps with a new name, structure, incorporation or area` THEN
        IF `the members are substantially the same` AND `the purposes are substantially the same`
        THEN `yes: today's institution is the same institution, as the class or type of its members and its primary purposes or work are substantially the same (s 50R(1), (2)), whatever changed in its name, structure, incorporation or area (s 50R(3))`
        ELSE `yes, if the court finds today's institution substantially the same as it was when the cause of action accrued (s 50R(1)); the sufficient test of s 50R(2) is not met on these facts`
    WHEN `it ceased, with no successor` THEN `the Act does not say: with no institution the same or substantially the same, and no relevant successor, s 50R names no one`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the number of successors` GREATER THAN 1
        THEN `yes: each of the relevant successors is jointly and severally liable for the abuse, and each may recover contribution from the others (s 50R(6))`
        ELSE `yes: today's institution is a relevant successor of the old institution, and is taken to be the same institution (s 50R(4), (5))`

§§ `s 50B -- associated trusts`

-- s 50B(1): "a trust is an associated trust of an institution if the institution uses the trust to carry out its
-- functions or activities and -- (a) the institution has, directly or indirectly, any of the following powers: (i) ...
-- control the application of income ... or the distribution of property ...; (ii) ... obtain the beneficial enjoyment
-- ...; (iii) ... appoint or remove a trustee or beneficiary ...; (iv) ... determine the outcome of any other decision
-- about the trust's operations; or (b) a member or manager of the institution has, under the trust deed ..., a power
-- mentioned in paragraph (a); or (c) a trustee is accustomed to acting, or is under a formal or informal obligation to
-- act, according to the directions, instructions or wishes of the institution or a member or manager". (2): in Divisions
-- 5 and 6 it includes a trust for which a s 50J(5) order is in force.
DECLARE `Trust facts` HAS
    `the institution uses the trust for its functions or activities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the institution has a power over the trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a member or manager has such a power under the trust deed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee acts on the institution's directions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a s 50J(5) order is in force for it` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Trust answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an associated trust of the institution (s 50B(1))`
    `yes, for Divisions 5 and 6 (paying an abuse claim): a court order under s 50J(5) is in force for it (s 50B(2))`
    `no: a trust is an associated trust only if the institution uses it to carry out its functions or activities (s 50B(1))`
    `no: the institution uses the trust, but neither it nor a member or manager has a power over the trust listed in s 50B(1)(a), and the trustee does not act on their directions (s 50B(1)(c))`

GIVEN t IS A `Trust facts`
GIVETH A `Trust answer`
`the trust answer for` t MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF t's `the institution uses the trust for its functions or activities`
           AND (t's `the institution has a power over the trust` OR t's `a member or manager has such a power under the trust deed` OR t's `the trustee acts on the institution's directions`)
        THEN `yes: an associated trust of the institution (s 50B(1))`
        IF t's `a s 50J(5) order is in force for it`
        THEN `yes, for Divisions 5 and 6 (paying an abuse claim): a court order under s 50J(5) is in force for it (s 50B(2))`
        IF (NOT (t's `the institution uses the trust for its functions or activities`))
        THEN `no: a trust is an associated trust only if the institution uses it to carry out its functions or activities (s 50B(1))`
        OTHERWISE `no: the institution uses the trust, but neither it nor a member or manager has a power over the trust listed in s 50B(1)(a), and the trustee does not act on their directions (s 50B(1)(c))`

§§ `ss 50L-50P -- out of what a judgment or settlement may be paid`

-- s 50L(2): the institution "may satisfy the liability out of the assets of the institution and the assets of an
-- associated trust"; s 50M(2): a nominee that is the trustee of an associated trust, "out of the assets of the trust and
-- the assets of the institution"; (3) any other nominee, "out of its assets and the assets of the institution"; s 50N(2):
-- the current office holder "is not personally liable but may satisfy the liability out of the assets of the institution
-- and the assets of an associated trust"; s 50O(4): the trustee's liability as nominee "is limited to the value of the
-- trust property"; s 50P: the liability includes the costs of the proceeding.
DECLARE `Liable party` IS ONE OF
    `the institution`
    `the institution's nominee, which is the trustee of an associated trust of the institution`
    `the institution's nominee, which is not the trustee of an associated trust`
    `the current office holder, sued in the name of the office`

DECLARE `Asset source` IS ONE OF
    `the institution's assets`
    `the assets of an associated trust of the institution`
    `the assets of the trust of which the nominee is trustee, the trustee being liable only up to the value of the trust property (ss 50M(2), 50O(4))`
    `the nominee's own assets`
    `not the current office holder's own assets: they are not personally liable (s 50N(2))`

GIVEN p IS A `Liable party`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Asset source`
`the assets for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the institution` THEN LIST `the institution's assets`, `the assets of an associated trust of the institution`
    WHEN `the institution's nominee, which is the trustee of an associated trust of the institution` THEN LIST `the assets of the trust of which the nominee is trustee, the trustee being liable only up to the value of the trust property (ss 50M(2), 50O(4))`, `the institution's assets`
    WHEN `the institution's nominee, which is not the trustee of an associated trust` THEN LIST `the nominee's own assets`, `the institution's assets`
    WHEN `the current office holder, sued in the name of the office` THEN LIST `the institution's assets`, `the assets of an associated trust of the institution`, `not the current office holder's own assets: they are not personally liable (s 50N(2))`

§§ `s 50J(5), (6) -- asking for a trust's trustee to be made the institution's nominee`

-- s 50J(5): "On application by the claimant, a court may order that the trustee of a trust is the institution's nominee
-- if the court is satisfied -- (a) the trust is, or used to be, an associated trust ...; and (b) for a trust that is no
-- longer an associated trust ... -- a reason for causing the trust to cease to be an associated trust was to try to
-- avoid trust property being applied to satisfy a liability ...; and (c) the order would be appropriate." (6):
-- "Subsection (5) applies if -- (a) at least 120 days have passed since a proceeding for an abuse claim was commenced
-- against the institution; and (b) either -- (i) there is no nominee for the institution; or (ii) a court is satisfied
-- the institution's nominee does not have sufficient assets ...". Fork F6: 120 days "have passed" on the 120th day after
-- the day the proceeding was commenced.
DECLARE `Nominee order facts` HAS
    `the institution is unincorporated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the proceeding was commenced` IS A DATE
    `the day of asking` IS A DATE
    `there is a nominee already` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nominee lacks sufficient assets` IS A `Court finding`
    `the trust is an associated trust now` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trust used to be an associated trust` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reason it ceased was to avoid abuse claims` IS A `Court finding`
    `the order would be appropriate` IS A `Court finding`

DECLARE `Nominee order answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: s 50J applies only to an institution that is an unincorporated body (s 50J(1))`
    `not yet: s 50J(5) applies once at least 120 days have passed since the proceeding was commenced (s 50J(6)(a)); they will have passed on` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE
    `no: there is a nominee, and the court is not satisfied that it lacks sufficient assets to meet the claim (s 50J(6)(b))`
    `no: the trust is not, and never was, an associated trust of the institution (s 50J(5)(a))`
    `no: the trust is no longer an associated trust, and the court is not satisfied that a reason it ceased was to keep its property from meeting an abuse claim (s 50J(5)(b))`
    `no: the court is not satisfied that the order would be appropriate (s 50J(5)(c))`
    `yes: the court is satisfied of everything s 50J(5) and (6) need, and may order that the trustee is the institution's nominee (s 50J(5))`
    `yes, you may apply: the court may order that the trustee is the institution's nominee if it is satisfied of the matters still to be decided in s 50J(5) and (6)(b)(ii)`

GIVEN n IS A `Nominee order facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `everything needed is found for` n IF
        ((NOT (n's `there is a nominee already`)) OR `is found` (n's `the nominee lacks sufficient assets`))
    AND (n's `the trust is an associated trust now` OR `is found` (n's `a reason it ceased was to avoid abuse claims`))
    AND `is found` (n's `the order would be appropriate`)
    WHERE
        `is found` x MEANS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN `the court has found that it is so` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN x IS A `Court finding`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is refused` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `the court has found that it is not so` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN n IS A `Nominee order facts`
GIVETH A `Nominee order answer`
`the nominee order answer for` n MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (n's `the institution is unincorporated`))
        THEN `no: s 50J applies only to an institution that is an unincorporated body (s 50J(1))`
        IF ((n's `the day of asking`) `is before` `the 120 days end`)
        THEN `not yet: s 50J(5) applies once at least 120 days have passed since the proceeding was commenced (s 50J(6)(a)); they will have passed on` `the 120 days end`
        IF n's `there is a nominee already` AND `is refused` (n's `the nominee lacks sufficient assets`)
        THEN `no: there is a nominee, and the court is not satisfied that it lacks sufficient assets to meet the claim (s 50J(6)(b))`
        IF (NOT (n's `the trust is an associated trust now`)) AND (NOT (n's `the trust used to be an associated trust`))
        THEN `no: the trust is not, and never was, an associated trust of the institution (s 50J(5)(a))`
        IF (NOT (n's `the trust is an associated trust now`)) AND `is refused` (n's `a reason it ceased was to avoid abuse claims`)
        THEN `no: the trust is no longer an associated trust, and the court is not satisfied that a reason it ceased was to keep its property from meeting an abuse claim (s 50J(5)(b))`
        IF `is refused` (n's `the order would be appropriate`)
        THEN `no: the court is not satisfied that the order would be appropriate (s 50J(5)(c))`
        IF `everything needed is found for` n
        THEN `yes: the court is satisfied of everything s 50J(5) and (6) need, and may order that the trustee is the institution's nominee (s 50J(5))`
        OTHERWISE `yes, you may apply: the court may order that the trustee is the institution's nominee if it is satisfied of the matters still to be decided in s 50J(5) and (6)(b)(ii)`
    WHERE
        `the 120 days end` MEANS (n's `the day the proceeding was commenced`) `plus days` 120

§§ `s 50J(7)(a) -- the court's order to identify associated trusts (a regulative rule)`

-- s 50J(7): "A court may -- (a) order the institution to do the following within 28 days or any other period the court
-- considers appropriate: (i) identify to the court any trusts that are, or used to be, associated trusts of the
-- institution; (ii) provide particular information about the financial capacity of the trusts". Once the order is made,
-- the institution must comply within the period; the claimant can state the order's day and period and whether, and
-- when, it complied. The period counts from the day of the order, that day not counted (fork F7).
DECLARE `Order party` IS ONE OF `the institution`, `the claimant`

DECLARE `Order act` IS ONE OF
    `identify its associated trusts and give the information about their financial capacity`

GIVEN `the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Order party` `Order act`
`the order to identify associated trusts within` `the period` MEANS
    PARTY `the institution`
    MUST `identify its associated trusts and give the information about their financial capacity`
    WITHIN `the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the institution` BECAUSE "the institution did not identify its associated trusts and their financial capacity within the period the court ordered (s 50J(7)(a))"

`the period the Act names` MEANS 28

GIVEN `another period was set` IS A BOOLEAN, `the days set` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the period ordered` `another period was set` `the days set` MEANS
    IF `another period was set` THEN `the days set` ELSE `the period the Act names`

DECLARE `Compliance answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the institution complied on or before the last day`
    `late: the institution complied after the last day`
    `still in time: the institution has not complied yet, and the last day has not passed`
    `late: the institution has not complied, and the last day has passed`

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED
-- means in time and anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it today would still be in
-- time. It takes plain facts only.
GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `the period` IS A NUMBER
      `it has complied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it complied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Compliance answer`
`the compliance answer for the order of` `the day of the order` `within` `the period` `complied` `it has complied` `on` `the day it complied` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has complied`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the order to identify associated trusts within` `the period`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the institution` `identify its associated trusts and give the information about their financial capacity` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `the day it complied`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `in time: the institution complied on or before the last day`
         OTHERWISE `late: the institution complied after the last day`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`the order to identify associated trusts within` `the period`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the institution` `identify its associated trusts and give the information about their financial capacity` (`the days from` `the day of the order` `to` `today`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still in time: the institution has not complied yet, and the last day has not passed`
         OTHERWISE `late: the institution has not complied, and the last day has passed`

§§ `s 50U -- proceedings despite an earlier judgment that the defendant was not appropriate`

-- s 50U(1): "proceedings on a cause of action may be commenced against a person or institution in accordance with this
-- Part even though a judgment was given in relation to the cause of action before the commencement of this Part on the
-- ground that the person or institution was not an appropriate defendant." (2): "may only be commenced if a court, being
-- satisfied that it is just and reasonable to do so, grants leave". A judgment on or after 1 August 2022 is outside the
-- period the text fixes, so the answer is no (the 2026-11-05 ruling (a)).
DECLARE `Earlier judgment answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court has granted leave, being satisfied that it is just and reasonable (s 50U(2))`
    `not without leave: you may commence the proceedings only if a court, satisfied that it is just and reasonable, grants leave (s 50U(1), (2))`
    `no: the court did not grant leave, and the proceedings may only be commenced with it (s 50U(2))`
    `no: s 50U covers only a judgment given before 1 August 2022, when Part 7A came into operation (s 50U(1))`
    `s 50U does not arise: there was no earlier judgment that the defendant was not an appropriate defendant`

GIVEN `there was such a judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the judgment` IS A DATE
      `leave` IS A `Court finding`
GIVETH AN `Earlier judgment answer`
`the earlier judgment answer for` `there was such a judgment` `on` `the day of the judgment` `with leave` `leave` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `there was such a judgment`)
        THEN `s 50U does not arise: there was no earlier judgment that the defendant was not an appropriate defendant`
        IF (NOT (`the day of the judgment` `is before` `the commencement of Part 7A`))
        THEN `no: s 50U covers only a judgment given before 1 August 2022, when Part 7A came into operation (s 50U(1))`
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `leave`
             WHEN `the court has found that it is so` THEN `yes: the court has granted leave, being satisfied that it is just and reasonable (s 50U(2))`
             WHEN `the court has found that it is not so` THEN `no: the court did not grant leave, and the proceedings may only be commenced with it (s 50U(2))`
             OTHERWISE `not without leave: you may commence the proceedings only if a court, satisfied that it is just and reasonable, grants leave (s 50U(1), (2))`

§§ `Part 7B, s 50V -- affected agreements`

-- s 50V(1): "affected agreement means an agreement -- (a) that prevents the commencement or maintenance of proceedings
-- on a cause of action to which section 3A of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936 applies if -- (i) the agreement occurred
-- before the commencement of that section; and (ii) at the time of the agreement, a limitation period applying to the
-- cause of action had expired; or (b) that prevents the commencement or maintenance of proceedings on a cause of action
-- in respect of an abuse claim (within the meaning of Part 7A) if -- (i) the agreement occurred before the commencement
-- of Part 7A; and (ii) at the time of the agreement, proceedings on the cause of action could not be commenced or
-- maintained against a person or institution that would have been liable under Part 7A for child abuse had the Part
-- been in force." (2): a limitation period counts as expired "even if it were possible at the time to seek the leave of
-- a court to extend the period."
--
-- Fork F8: "a cause of action to which section 3A ... applies" is borrowed from the Limitation of Actions Act 1936 and
-- worked out here from the same facts, because the stable l4 cannot IMPORT that Act's encoding: an action for damages
-- relating to death or personal injury resulting from abuse when the person was a child (under 18), abuse there
-- "including" the same three kinds as s 50A here.
DECLARE `Agreement facts` HAS
    `the abuse facts` IS AN `Abuse facts`
    `the claim is for damages for personal injury or death` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement prevents proceedings on the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE
    `a limitation period had expired then` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no one liable under Part 7A could then be sued` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN a IS AN `Agreement facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`limb (a) holds for` a MEANS
    IF     `a child at age` (a's `the abuse facts`'s `the age when abused`)
       AND a's `the claim is for damages for personal injury or death`
       AND ((a's `the day of the agreement`) `is before` `the commencement of section 3A of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936`)
       AND a's `a limitation period had expired then`
    THEN IF `is a kind of abuse the Act lists` (a's `the abuse facts`'s `the abuse`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN a IS AN `Agreement facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`limb (b) holds for` a MEANS
    IF ((a's `the day of the agreement`) `is before` `the commencement of Part 7A`) AND a's `no one liable under Part 7A could then be sued`
    THEN CONSIDER `the claim status of` (a's `the abuse facts`)
         WHEN `an abuse claim` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `not an abuse claim` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Affected agreement answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an affected agreement, made before 1 February 2019 when a limitation period on your claim for child abuse had already expired (s 50V(1)(a), (2))`
    `yes: an affected agreement, made before 1 August 2022 when no one who would have been liable under Part 7A could be sued (s 50V(1)(b))`
    `yes: an affected agreement on both grounds (s 50V(1)(a) and (b))`
    `no: an affected agreement is one that prevents you from commencing or maintaining proceedings on the claim (s 50V(1))`
    `no: not an affected agreement, as it meets neither s 50V(1)(a) (made before 1 February 2019 on a child abuse claim whose limitation period had expired) nor s 50V(1)(b) (made before 1 August 2022 on an abuse claim when no one liable under Part 7A could be sued)`
    `the Act does not say: whether it is an affected agreement turns on an open list of what abuse, or who is associated with an institution, includes (s 3A(5) of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936; ss 50A, 50C)`

GIVEN a IS AN `Agreement facts`
GIVETH AN `Affected agreement answer`
`the affected agreement answer for` a MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (a's `the agreement prevents proceedings on the claim`))
        THEN `no: an affected agreement is one that prevents you from commencing or maintaining proceedings on the claim (s 50V(1))`
        IF `is true` (`limb (a) holds for` a) AND `is true` (`limb (b) holds for` a)
        THEN `yes: an affected agreement on both grounds (s 50V(1)(a) and (b))`
        IF `is true` (`limb (a) holds for` a)
        THEN `yes: an affected agreement, made before 1 February 2019 when a limitation period on your claim for child abuse had already expired (s 50V(1)(a), (2))`
        IF `is true` (`limb (b) holds for` a)
        THEN `yes: an affected agreement, made before 1 August 2022 when no one who would have been liable under Part 7A could be sued (s 50V(1)(b))`
        IF `is false` (`limb (a) holds for` a) AND `is false` (`limb (b) holds for` a)
        THEN `no: not an affected agreement, as it meets neither s 50V(1)(a) (made before 1 February 2019 on a child abuse claim whose limitation period had expired) nor s 50V(1)(b) (made before 1 August 2022 on an abuse claim when no one liable under Part 7A could be sued)`
        OTHERWISE `the Act does not say: whether it is an affected agreement turns on an open list of what abuse, or who is associated with an institution, includes (s 3A(5) of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936; ss 50A, 50C)`
    WHERE
        `is true` m MEANS
            CONSIDER m
            WHEN JUST b THEN b
            OTHERWISE FALSE
        `is false` m MEANS
            CONSIDER m
            WHEN JUST b THEN NOT b
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 50W -- setting an affected agreement aside`

-- s 50W(1): a person prevented by an affected agreement may "(a) commence proceedings on the cause of action in a court
-- with sufficient jurisdiction ...; and (b) apply to the court to set aside the affected agreement." (2): "The court may
-- set aside an affected agreement if it is just and reasonable to do so." (3) what the court may consider; (4) the
-- settlement negotiations may be put in evidence despite s 67C(1) of the Evidence Act 1929; (5) what gives effect to the
-- agreement may be set aside too; (6): "the court must not set aside ... (a) a deed of release signed by or on behalf of
-- the applicant in acceptance of an offer under the National Redress Scheme and an agreement relating to a relevant
-- prior payment that has been taken into account in the offer; (b) a contract of insurance."
DECLARE `Set aside answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the court has found it just and reasonable, and may set the agreement aside (s 50W(2)), with any contract, deed, order or judgment giving effect to it (s 50W(5))`
    `yes, if the court finds it just and reasonable: commence proceedings on the claim in a court with jurisdiction and apply to set the agreement aside (s 50W(1), (2)); the court may weigh the matters in s 50W(3), and the settlement negotiations may be put in evidence (s 50W(4))`
    `no: the court may set an affected agreement aside only if it is just and reasonable, and it found that it is not (s 50W(2))`
    `no: the court must not set aside a deed of release accepting an offer under the National Redress Scheme, or an agreement about a prior payment taken into account in that offer (s 50W(6)(a))`
    `no: the court must not set aside a contract of insurance (s 50W(6)(b))`
    `no: Part 7B sets aside only an affected agreement (ss 50V, 50W(1)); see the affected agreement question`
    `the Act does not say whether this is an affected agreement (see the affected agreement question)`

GIVEN a IS AN `Agreement facts`
      `it is a National Redress Scheme release` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a contract of insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `just and reasonable` IS A `Court finding`
GIVETH A `Set aside answer`
`the set aside answer for` a `redress release` `it is a National Redress Scheme release` `insurance` `it is a contract of insurance` `finding` `just and reasonable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the affected agreement answer for` a
    WHEN `the Act does not say: whether it is an affected agreement turns on an open list of what abuse, or who is associated with an institution, includes (s 3A(5) of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936; ss 50A, 50C)` THEN `the Act does not say whether this is an affected agreement (see the affected agreement question)`
    WHEN `no: an affected agreement is one that prevents you from commencing or maintaining proceedings on the claim (s 50V(1))` THEN `no: Part 7B sets aside only an affected agreement (ss 50V, 50W(1)); see the affected agreement question`
    WHEN `no: not an affected agreement, as it meets neither s 50V(1)(a) (made before 1 February 2019 on a child abuse claim whose limitation period had expired) nor s 50V(1)(b) (made before 1 August 2022 on an abuse claim when no one liable under Part 7A could be sued)` THEN `no: Part 7B sets aside only an affected agreement (ss 50V, 50W(1)); see the affected agreement question`
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            IF `it is a National Redress Scheme release`
            THEN `no: the court must not set aside a deed of release accepting an offer under the National Redress Scheme, or an agreement about a prior payment taken into account in that offer (s 50W(6)(a))`
            IF `it is a contract of insurance`
            THEN `no: the court must not set aside a contract of insurance (s 50W(6)(b))`
            OTHERWISE CONSIDER `just and reasonable`
                 WHEN `the court has found that it is so` THEN `yes: the court has found it just and reasonable, and may set the agreement aside (s 50W(2)), with any contract, deed, order or judgment giving effect to it (s 50W(5))`
                 WHEN `the court has found that it is not so` THEN `no: the court may set an affected agreement aside only if it is just and reasonable, and it found that it is not (s 50W(2))`
                 OTHERWISE `yes, if the court finds it just and reasonable: commence proceedings on the claim in a court with jurisdiction and apply to set the agreement aside (s 50W(1), (2)); the court may weigh the matters in s 50W(3), and the settlement negotiations may be put in evidence (s 50W(4))`

§§ `s 50X -- what follows when an agreement is set aside`

-- s 50X(1): the agreement and anything else set aside "is void". (2): "An amount paid or other consideration given
-- under the affected agreement -- (a) is not recoverable despite the agreement being void; and (b) may be taken into
-- account by the court in determining damages".
DECLARE `Repayment answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the agreement is void, but what you received under it cannot be recovered from you; the court may take it into account in assessing your damages (s 50X(1), (2))`
    `s 50X does not arise: the agreement has not been set aside under Part 7B`

GIVEN `it has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Repayment answer`
`the repayment answer` `it has been set aside` MEANS
    IF `it has been set aside`
    THEN `no: the agreement is void, but what you received under it cannot be recovered from you; the court may take it into account in assessing your damages (s 50X(1), (2))`
    ELSE `s 50X does not arise: the agreement has not been set aside under Part 7B`
